    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the power rule with $n=12$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{12}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{12+1}}{12+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{13}}{13})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{13}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{13})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot 13{x}^{12} & = \\\\ {x}^{12}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$",
